tasks.statement:
Add #[derive(Debug)] to the struct Book { title: &str, pages: u32 } and print the instance with {:?} and then prettily with {:#?}. For the book «Rust» with 500 pages: first «Book { title: "Rust", pages: 500 }», then the multi-line form.

Expected output:
Book { title: "Rust", pages: 500 }
Book {
    title: "Rust",
    pages: 500,
}

tasks.starter:
enum Color {
    Red,
    Green,
    Blue,
}

fn name(c: Color) -> &'static str {
    match c {
        Color::Red => "red",
        Color::Green => "green",
    }
}

fn main() {
    println!("{}", name(Color::Blue));
}
